[0.000, "o", "# nitpick: request changes\r\n\r\n`working tree vs HEAD` · branch `fix-ranges` · head `b7a4ac3` · 2 file(s) · ~7.8k tokens of context · 2/2 model(s) · 82.7s\r\n\r\n**stealth/space-bunny-alpha** (request changes, 24.2s, $0.0000): The change attempts to adjust diff ranges and path-stem extraction, but both introduce core context-selection regressions. Inclusive hunk ranges gain an extra line, while ordinary filenames are reduced to their extensions.\r\n\r\n**nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free** (request changes, 82.5s, $0.0000): Two changes: (1) diff.rs new_ranges() now returns end-exclusive ranges despite the doc saying inclusive, breaking an existing test. (2) search.rs path_stem() switched from split('.') to rsplit('.'), changing the stem for multi-dot filenames and breaking test-file detection logic in context.rs that relies on the old behavior.\r\n\r\n## Findings (3)\r\n\r\n### High\r\n\r\n- **src/diff.rs:59** new_ranges includes a line beyond each hunk `[bug]` (2/2 models)\r\n  The endpoint is still documented and tested"]
[0.000, "o", " as inclusive, but a hunk with `new_start = 10` and `new_len = 3` covers lines 10–12, not 10–13. This includes one unchanged trailing line in every context range and makes the existing assertions expecting `(1, 4)` and `(1, 2)` fail.\r\n  Suggestion: Keep the inclusive endpoint as `h.new_start + h.new_len - 1`; filtering `new_len > 0` already guarantees the subtraction is valid.\r\n- **src/search.rs:212** path_stem now returns the file extension `[bug]` (1/2 models)\r\n  `rsplit('.').next()` returns the text after the final dot, so `path_stem(\"src/app.rs\")` now returns `\"rs\"` rather than `\"app\"`. The changed-file symbol search at `src/context.rs:477` will consequently generate patterns from file extensions, and related-test matching will generally fail to associate `app.test.ts` with `app.ts`.\r\n  Suggestion: Restore `name.split('.').next().unwrap_or(name)` (or implement the exact intended stem semantics with tests covering names containing multiple dots).\r\n- **src/search.rs:212** path_stem() behavior change bre"]
[0.000, "o", "aks test-file detection in context.rs `[regression]` (1/2 models)\r\n  Changed from `split('.')` (first segment) to `rsplit('.')` (stem without last extension). For 'foo.test.rs', old stem='foo', new stem='foo.test'. The test detection logic in context.rs:696-704 uses the stem to match patterns like '{stem}.test.*', '{stem}_test.*', etc. With the new stem 'foo.test', it looks for 'foo.test.test.*' and misses 'foo.test.rs'. This is a silent regression in test-file discovery.\r\n  Suggestion: Either revert path_stem to split('.') for compatibility, or update context.rs test detection to work with the new stem definition (e.g., also check the old stem).\r\n\r\n3 finding(s) at or above `high`. Exit code 1.\r\n"]
